	<Language_en_US>
		<Replace Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_COCA">
			<Text>Coca</Text>
		</Replace>
		<Replace Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_COCA_TEXT">
			<Text>Coca is the leaf of any of four cultivated species of the family Erythroxylaceae native to western South America. The plant is famous for its various medicinal and nutritional uses, increasing alertness, dulling pain, supressing appetite, and treating altitude sickness. The leaves are traditionally chewed or brewed into a tea. Coca made an impression on the Spanish conquerors for its ability to help people work harder, even through exhaustion or hunger.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Today, coca is best known for its psychoactive alkaloid, cocaine. The alkaloid content of coca leaves is relatively low, requiring a large number of leaves for a single batch of cocaine. Coca leaf extract was once used widely in a wide range of medicinal and consumer products, but was later made a controlled substance and eliminated from North American and European consumer markets in the early 20th century.</Text>
		</Replace>
		<Replace Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_MONOPOLY_COMBAT_STRENGTH">
			<Text>[COLOR_POSITIVE_TEXT]Monopoly Bonus:[ENDCOLOR] +5% [ICON_STRENGTH] Combat Strength to all Units.</Text>
		</Replace>

		<Replace Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_REINDEER">
			<Text>Reindeer</Text>
		</Replace>
		<Replace Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_REINDEER_HELP">
			<Text></Text>
<!-- Is placed by the Reindeer District of [ICON_CULTURE_JFD_POLAR] [COLOR:182:17:254:255]{TXT_KEY_CULTURE_JFD_POLAR_SHORT_DESC}[ENDCOLOR] Civilizations on Tundra or Snow tiles. -->
		</Replace>
		<Replace Tag="TXT_KEY_CIV5_RESOURCE_REINDEER_TEXT">
			<Text>The reindeer or caribou is a species of deer with circumpolar distribution, native to Arctic, subarctic, tundra, boreal, and mountainous regions of Northern Europe, Siberia, and North America. Reindeer occur in both migratory and sedentary populations, and their herd sizes vary greatly in different regions. The tundra subspecies are adapted for extreme cold, and some are adapted for long-distance migration. They are unique among deer (Cervidae) in that females may have antlers. Reindeer are the only successfully semi-domesticated deer on a large scale in the world. Both wild and domestic reindeer have been an important source of food, clothing, and shelter for Arctic people from prehistorical times. They are still herded and hunted today.</Text>
		</Replace>

		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_MC_RUM">
			<Text>Liquor</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="TXT_KEY_RESOURCE_MC_RUM_PEDIA">
			<Text>Liquor, or spirits, are alcoholic drinks produced by the distillation of grains, fruits, vegetables, or sugar that have already gone through alcoholic fermentation. The distillation process concentrates the alcohol, so the resulting condensate has an increased alcohol by volume. Some examples of liquors include vodka, rum, gin and tequila. Liquors are often aged in barrels, such as for the production of brandy and whiskey, or are infused with flavorings to form flavored liquors, such as absinthe.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Is placed by the conversion of Bonus Resources by the Distillery Improvement of the [ICON_CULTURE_JFD_COLONIAL] [COLOR:182:17:254:255]{TXT_KEY_CULTURE_JFD_COLONIAL_SHORT_DESC}[ENDCOLOR] Cultural Group.</Text>
		</Row>
	</Language_en_US>
